module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallZariskiRealFullyFaithful
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesUnderComparison
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The global types of modules under `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` on the small Zariski site

Descent, Lemma 05VG compares fifteen properties of modules across the two equivalences
`QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` and `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`, `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, of
Descent, Proposition 03DX.  Definition 03DU gives a small site only for `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale}`,
so the second functor is quantified over those two topologies alone.

**This file settles the seven global clauses of Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE for the small
site at `τ = Zariski`**, at the comparison functor of 03DX itself and with no quasi-coherence
hypothesis at all.

## Why it costs nothing here

`𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` at `τ = Zariski` on the small site is the pullback of sheaves of modules along the
morphism of ringed sites of Remark 03FH, which at that `τ` is an *equivalence* of ringed sites:
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isEquivalence_associatedModuleOfSheaf` makes it an equivalence
of the whole module categories, not merely of the quasi-coherent ones.  An equivalence is full,
faithful and preserves all colimits, and it carries the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf
by `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit`; those are exactly the
hypotheses under which
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesUnderComparison` proves the seven
global clauses for an abstract comparison functor.  So each statement below is that file's
theorem instantiated, and the quasi-coherence that 05VG's source category carries is not needed.

## The eight local clauses, and why they are not here

They are not reached, and the reason is worth recording because a tempting reading appears to
reach them.  That reading takes `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` at `τ = Zariski` to be
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModuleOfIdentity`, the pullback along the *identity*
morphism of ringed sites of `(S_Zar, 𝒪_S)`, which is isomorphic to the identity functor of
`Mod(S_Zar, 𝒪_S)`.  Under that reading `𝓕` and `𝓕^a` are isomorphic objects of one and the same
category, so every one of the fifteen properties transfers by pure invariance under
isomorphism — including the four that this development can transport in no other way.  But that
reading is not the functor of Definition 03DU (4): the coefficient sheaf of the small Zariski
site is `T/S ↦ Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`, which is isomorphic to `𝒪_S` and not equal to it, so the identity
functor states something else.  The real comparison, used here, is a functor **between two
different categories over two different sites**, `Mod(S_Zar, 𝒪_S) ⥤ Mod(S_Zar, 𝒪)`.

Across that functor a *global* clause still costs nothing, being a condition on the module
alone.  A *local* clause is not: it quantifies over the objects of the site and over coverings
of them, so transporting it means carrying covering data across the underlying equivalence of
sites, and invariance under isomorphism says nothing about that.  The local clauses therefore
genuinely used that the comparison was the identity and not merely that it was an equivalence,
and they are left open here:

* **03DL (4), (5) and (7)** — locally generated by `r` sections, finite type, finite
  presentation — are *reachable*, by a route this file does not take, and have since been
  reached: they hold for a comparison carried as an equivalence of ringed **topoi**, the small
  Zariski site is the one case of 05VG whose comparison morphism of ringed topoi *is* an
  equivalence, and the packaging that was missing — exhibiting Remark 03FH's morphism as an
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom` whose pushforward is an equivalence and whose structure map
  is invertible — is now
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.toOpensRingedToposHom`.  The three clauses are in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallZariskiLocalTypesComparison`.
* **03ER (3)**, flat, is *not* reachable that way, and the packaging is not what blocks it.
  Stacks 05VD, `Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.isFlat_pullbackModules`, requires its source
  ringed topos to have its object universe equal to the universe of the sections of its
  structure sheaf, and the small Zariski ringed topos is a `RingedTopos.{u, u + 1, u}`.  What is
  needed is 05VD with those two universes independent.
* **03DL (2)**, finite locally free, has a transport along an equivalence of ringed *sites* —
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_reindex_iff`
  (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FiniteLocallyFreeSiteComparison.lean:271`) — but that
  is stated for `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.reindex`, which transports the structure sheaf
  along the site equivalence and then pushes the module forward along the *identity*.
  Identifying it with the pullback along `structureMap`, whose structure-sheaf comparison
  `AlgebraicGeometry.smallZariskiStructureSheaf_iso` is not the identity, is the step not taken.
* **03DL (1)**, locally free, which 05VG excepts, **03DL (3)**, locally generated by sections,
  and **03DL (8)**, coherent, have no transport of any kind in this development; the reasons are
  recorded in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesUnderComparison`.

The invariance-under-isomorphism lemmas that reading would rest on are functor-agnostic and
live in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderIso`.

